# Communications 1: Modulation and Detection

A digital link turns bits into symbols, symbols into a waveform, sends the waveform through a noisy channel, and then decides what was sent. This chapter builds that chain on complete blocks of data: constellations and the mapping of bits to symbols, noise at a chosen energy per bit and the decisions that follow (hard bits and soft likelihood ratios) with their error rate against theory, pulse shaping with matched filtering, OFDM over a multipath channel, convolutional coding with Viterbi decoding, and timing and carrier synchronisation.

- [Constellations and mapping](comms_01_modulation/constellations_and_mapping.md)
- [Noise and detection](comms_01_modulation/noise_and_detection.md)
- [Pulse shaping](comms_01_modulation/pulse_shaping.md)
- [OFDM and multipath](comms_01_modulation/ofdm.md)
- [Channel coding](comms_01_modulation/channel_coding.md)
- [LDPC and turbo codes](comms_01_modulation/iterative_codes.md)
- [Synchronisation](comms_01_modulation/synchronisation.md)
